The reason we have added a second constructor that takes no parameters is so
that MongoDB can deserialize WorkItem.
During deserialization, an instance of the object is created. As a result, a
parameterless constructor is necessary; otherwise, the deserialization
would be unable to create the object (as it has no way of determining the
relevant parameters.)
